      "writtenOn": "2023-05-08T15:18:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking closer at the [ppc_chips[]](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/ppc.c;l\u003d52) definition, it looks like array size will correctly get set to the number of `named-usbc-port` nodes found.\n\nIf one of the `named-usbc-port` entries omits the `ppc` property, then the `ppc_chips[]` will be set to NULL for that entry.\n\nSo I\u0027m backtracking on my suggestion.  I think putting `is-alt` on all the PPCs, and then using PPC_ENABLE_ALTERNATE_BY_NODELABEL to install the correct PPC at runtime as appropriate.\n\nLonger term, I\u0027m plan to propose a common devicetree property \"deferred-init`, which would do something similar as the `is-alt` property.",
